7 1 Education;SpecialEducation;StateAid. AmendRSA186-C:18,III(a)-(b)toreadasfollows:
8 III.(a) The state board of education through the commissioner, department of education,
9 shall distribute aid available under this paragraph as entitlement to such school districts as have a
10 special education pupil for whose costs they are responsible, for whom the costs of special education
11 in the fiscal year exceed 3 and 1/2 times the estimated state average expenditure per pupil for the
12 school year preceding the year of distribution. [If in any year, the amount appropriated for
13 distribution as special education aid in accordance with this section is insufficient therefor, the
14 appropriation shall be prorated proportionally based on entitlement among the districts entitled to a
15 grant.] If in any year, the amountappropriated for distribution as special education aid in
16 accordance with this section is insufficient therefor, the appropriation shall be prorated
17 proportionally based on entitlement among the districts entitled to a grant, provided that
18 the department of education shall distribute to the school district not less than 80 percent
19 of the district’s entitlement for catastrophic aid costs in the fiscal year. If there are
20 unexpended funds appropriated under this paragraph at the end of any fiscal year, such funds shall
21 be distributed for court-ordered placements and episodes of treatment under RSA 186-C:19-b. The
22 state may designate up to $250,000 of the funds which are appropriated as required by this
23 paragraph,foreachfiscalyear,toassistthoseschooldistrictswhich,underguidelinesestablishedby
24 rules of the state board of education, may qualify for emergency assistance to mitigate the impact of
25 specialeducationcosts. Thestatemaydesignateuptoanadditional$250,000ofthefundswhichare
26 appropriatedunderthisparagraphforeachfiscalyearforanycommunityof1,000orfewerresidents
27 to mitigate the impact of special education costs when emergency assistance is necessary to prevent
28 significant financial harm to such district or community. Upon application to the commissioner of
29 education, and approval by the commissioner, such funds may be accepted and expended by school
30 districts in accordance with this chapter; provided, however, that if a school district has received
31 emergency assistance funds for certain children with disabilities, it shall not receive special
32 educationaid for thosesamechildrenwithdisabilities. If anyof thefunds designated for emergency
