8 2 Education;SpecialEducation;StateAid. AmendRSA186-C:18,IVtoreadasfollows:
9 IV. [The state shall appropriate an amount for each fiscal year to assist special education
10 programs that are statewide in their scope, and that meet the standards for such programs
11 established by the state board of education. Funds under this paragraph shall be administered and
12 distributed by the state board of education through the commissioner.] The amount necessary to
13 fund special education aid under this section is hereby appropriated to the department
14 from the education trust fund created under RSA 198:39. The governor is authorized to
15 draw a warrant from the education trust fund to satisfy the state's obligation under this
16 section. Such warrant for payment shall be issued regardless of the balance of funds
17 available in the education trust fund. If the balance in the education trust fund, after the
18 issuance of any such warrant, is less than zero, the state comptroller shall transfer
19 sufficient funds from the general fund to eliminate such deficit. The commissioner of the
20 department of administrative services shall inform the fiscal committee and the governor
21 and council of such balance. This reporting shall not in any way prohibit or delay the
22 distributionofpayments.
